==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|acerbité}}, from {{uder|en|la|acerbitās||acerbity; harshness}}, from {{m|la|acerbus||bitter}}. See {{m|en|acerb}}.
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈsɜːbɪti/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|en-uk-acerbity.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈsɝbɪti/|[əˈsɝbɪɾi]|a=US,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-acerbity.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈsɜːbɪti/|[əˈsɜːbɪɾi]|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[sourness|Sourness]] of taste, with [[bitterness]] and [[astringency]], like that of [[unripe]] fruit.
# [[harshness|Harshness]], bitterness, or severity
#: {{ux|en|'''acerbity''' of temper, of language, of pain}}
#* {{RQ:Orczy Miss Elliott|chapter=1|passage=“Well ?” I repeated with some '''acerbity'''. I had been wondering for the last ten minutes how many more knots he would manage to make in that same bit of string before he actually started undoing them again.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Something [[harsh]] ([[e.g.]] a [[remark]], [[act]] or [[experience]]).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1848|author=w:Elizabeth Gaskell|title=w:Mary Barton|location=London|publisher=Chapman and Hall|volume=2|chapter=16|page=222|url=https://archive.org/details/marybartonbyecg00bartgoog/page/n227/mode/1up?q=acerbities
|passage={{...}} the recollection of that yesterday {{...}} made him bear with the meekness and patience of a true-hearted man all the worrying little '''acerbities''' of to-day;}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1980|author=w:Anthony Burgess|title=w:Earthly Powers|url=https://archive.org/details/earthlypowers0000burg/page/115/mode/1up?q=acerbities|chapter=21|page=115|publisher=Penguin|year_published=1981
|passage=This opera was mainly in the style of late Puccini, with '''acerbities''' stolen from Stravinsky.}}

